---
permalink: /cocktails/search.json
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  What the "search for anything" box searches on a drink page (#1050): the
  drinks' half of food/search.json, whose comment gives the shape and the
  reasoning. Fetched by assets/js/page-search.js from the box
  _includes/page-search.html renders on every drink page.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  THE SAME LIST THE INDEX SHOWS. `all_drinks` is assembled as
  cocktails/index.html assembles it: the gated public collection, plus the
  drafts only under `site.show_drafts`, which _config_local.yml declares and
  production does not (#235). tests/test_rendered_pages.py holds the two lists
  equal in a production build.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  WHAT A DRINK CARRIES. `moods` is the drink's mood list, which the MOOD and
  HASSLE groups both count (one filter with two headings, MANUAL §9.13; the
  split is taxonomy.yml's `mood_groups`). `ing` is the card's ingredient line,
  label for label, from _plugins/cocktail_card_ingredients.rb, so a word
  chosen here is a chip the index's HAS TO HAVE field can apply (MANUAL §9.10.1).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  A JOINED "X OR Y" LABEL IS OFFERED AS ITS PARTS (#1130). The card prints
  "cherry brandy or cherry liqueur", which names no single chip (the `?ing=`
  grammar matches a chip whole, MANUAL §13.13), so a row offers
  `ing.search_labels` instead: one per generic, from the same `card_names` map
  the chips are built from. A disjunctive `generic` means either would do
  (#441), and `buildPool` in cocktail-search.js already adds a chip per generic.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  IT FAILS OPEN. The `if` below falls back to `ing.label` whenever
  `search_labels` is missing, so a `jekyll serve` started before the plugin
  gained the field (MANUAL §1: plugins are not reloaded) still offers every
  drink's ingredients rather than an empty list.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  `items_label` is the name search's own heading, I KNOW WHAT I WANT, as
  cocktails/index.html words it: each dropdown heading is the index section a
  result lands on (DECISIONS §13). food/search.json says the same.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign this_site = site.data.sites[page.site_key] -%}
{%- assign groups = site.data.cocktails.taxonomy.mood_groups -%}
{%- assign all_drinks = site.cocktail_recipes -%}
{%- if site.show_drafts -%}
  {%- assign all_drinks = all_drinks | concat: site.cocktail_drafts -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign sorted_drinks = all_drinks | sort: "title" -%}
{
  "site": {{ page.site_key | jsonify }},
  "home": {{ this_site.home | relative_url | jsonify }},
  "items_label": "I know what I want",
  "groups": [
    {"kind": "mood", "label": "Mood", "param": "mood", "field": "moods", "values": {{ groups.mood | jsonify }}},
    {"kind": "hassle", "label": "Hassle", "param": "mood", "field": "moods", "values": {{ groups.hassle | jsonify }}},
    {"kind": "ingredient", "label": "Has to have", "param": "ing", "field": "ing"}
  ],
  "items": [
    {%- for d in sorted_drinks %}
    {% unless forloop.first %},{% endunless %}{"t": {{ d.title | jsonify }}, "u": {{ d.url | relative_url | jsonify }}, "moods": {{ d.mood | jsonify }}, "ing": [{%- assign _first_ing = true -%}{%- for ing in d.card_ingredients -%}{%- if ing.search_labels -%}{%- for _l in ing.search_labels -%}{%- unless _first_ing %}, {% endunless -%}{{ _l | jsonify }}{%- assign _first_ing = false -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- else -%}{%- unless _first_ing %}, {% endunless -%}{{ ing.label | jsonify }}{%- assign _first_ing = false -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}]}
    {%- endfor %}
  ]
}
